{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '118,134p' ../agent-source/raftpb/raft.proto; sed -n '218,230p' ../agent-source/node.go; sed -n '77,116p' ../agent-source/raftpb/confchange.go; sed -n '270,350p' ../agent-source/confchange/confchange.go; sed -n '1,115p' ../agent-source/confchange/restore.go\"","aggregated_output":"enum ConfChangeTransition {\n\t// Automatically use the simple protocol if possible, otherwise fall back\n\t// to ConfChangeJointImplicit. Most applications will want to use this.\n\tConfChangeTransitionAuto          = 0;\n\t// Use joint consensus unconditionally, and transition out of them\n\t// automatically (by proposing a zero configuration change).\n\t//\n\t// This option is suitable for applications that want to minimize the time\n\t// spent in the joint configuration and do not store the joint configuration\n\t// in the state machine (outside of InitialState).\n\tConfChangeTransitionJointImplicit = 1;\n\t// Use joint consensus and remain in the joint configuration until the\n\t// application proposes a no-op configuration change. This is suitable for\n\t// applications that want to explicitly control the transitions, for example\n\t// to use a custom payload (via the Context field).\n\tConfChangeTransitionJointExplicit = 2;\n}\n\t// ReadIndex request a read state. The read state will be set in the ready.\n\t// Read state has a read index. Once the application advances further than the read\n\t// index, any linearizable read requests issued before the read request can be\n\t// processed safely. The read state will have the same rctx attached.\n\t// Note that request can be lost without notice, therefore it is user's job\n\t// to retry ReadIndex.\n\t//\n\t// Retries must always use new rctxes, and never reuse an rctx already\n\t// passed into ReadIndex. Starting with release-3.7, this restriction is\n\t// lifted, and it is ok to retry the same rctx. Refer to\n\t// https://github.com/etcd-io/raft/issues/392 for more details.\n\tReadIndex(ctx context.Context, rctx []byte) error\n\n// EnterJoint returns two bools. The second bool is true if and only if this\n// config change will use Joint Consensus, which is the case if it contains more\n// than one change or if the use of Joint Consensus was requested explicitly.\n// The first bool can only be true if second one is, and indicates whether the\n// Joint State will be left automatically.\nfunc (c ConfChangeV2) EnterJoint() (autoLeave bool, ok bool) {\n\t// NB: in theory, more config changes could qualify for the \"simple\"\n\t// protocol but it depends on the config on top of which the changes apply.\n\t// For example, adding two learners is not OK if both nodes are part of the\n\t// base config (i.e. two voters are turned into learners in the process of\n\t// applying the conf change). In practice, these distinctions should not\n\t// matter, so we keep it simple and use Joint Consensus liberally.\n\tif c.Transition != ConfChangeTransitionAuto || len(c.Changes) > 1 {\n\t\t// Use Joint Consensus.\n\t\tvar autoLeave bool\n\t\tswitch c.Transition {\n\t\tcase ConfChangeTransitionAuto:\n\t\t\tautoLeave = true\n\t\tcase ConfChangeTransitionJointImplicit:\n\t\t\tautoLeave = true\n\t\tcase ConfChangeTransitionJointExplicit:\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\tpanic(fmt.Sprintf(\"unknown transition: %+v\", c))\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn autoLeave, true\n\t}\n\treturn false, false\n}\n\n// LeaveJoint is true if the configuration change leaves a joint configuration.\n// This is the case if the ConfChangeV2 is zero, with the possible exception of\n// the Context field.\nfunc (c ConfChangeV2) LeaveJoint() bool {\n\t// NB: c is already a copy.\n\tc.Context = nil\n\treturn proto.Equal(&c, &ConfChangeV2{})\n}\n\n// ConfChangesFromString parses a Space-delimited sequence of operations into a\n// slice of ConfChangeSingle. The supported operations are:\n\t}\n}\n\n// checkInvariants makes sure that the config and progress are compatible with\n// each other. This is used to check both what the Changer is initialized with,\n// as well as what it returns.\nfunc checkInvariants(cfg tracker.Config, trk tracker.ProgressMap) error {\n\t// NB: intentionally allow the empty config. In production we'll never see a\n\t// non-empty config (we prevent it from being created) but we will need to\n\t// be able to *create* an initial config, for example during bootstrap (or\n\t// during tests). Instead of having to hand-code this, we allow\n\t// transitioning from an empty config into any other legal and non-empty\n\t// config.\n\tfor _, ids := range []map[uint64]struct{}{\n\t\tcfg.Voters.IDs(),\n\t\tcfg.Learners,\n\t\tcfg.LearnersNext,\n\t} {\n\t\tfor id := range ids {\n\t\t\tif _, ok := trk[id]; !ok {\n\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"no progress for %d\", id)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Any staged learner was staged because it could not be directly added due\n\t// to a conflicting voter in the outgoing config.\n\tfor id := range cfg.LearnersNext {\n\t\tif _, ok := outgoing(cfg.Voters)[id]; !ok {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%d is in LearnersNext, but not Voters[1]\", id)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif trk[id].IsLearner {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%d is in LearnersNext, but is already marked as learner\", id)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t// Conversely Learners and Voters doesn't intersect at all.\n\tfor id := range cfg.Learners {\n\t\tif _, ok := outgoing(cfg.Voters)[id]; ok {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%d is in Learners and Voters[1]\", id)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif _, ok := incoming(cfg.Voters)[id]; ok {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%d is in Learners and Voters[0]\", id)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !trk[id].IsLearner {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%d is in Learners, but is not marked as learner\", id)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tif !joint(cfg) {\n\t\t// We enforce that empty maps are nil instead of zero.\n\t\tif outgoing(cfg.Voters) != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cfg.Voters[1] must be nil when not joint\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tif cfg.LearnersNext != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cfg.LearnersNext must be nil when not joint\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tif cfg.AutoLeave {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"AutoLeave must be false when not joint\")\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// checkAndCopy copies the tracker's config and progress map (deeply enough for\n// the purposes of the Changer) and returns those copies. It returns an error\n// if checkInvariants does.\nfunc (c Changer) checkAndCopy() (tracker.Config, tracker.ProgressMap, error) {\n\tcfg := c.Tracker.Config.Clone()\n\ttrk := tracker.ProgressMap{}\n\n\tfor id, pr := range c.Tracker.Progress {\n\t\t// A shallow copy is enough because we only mutate the Learner field.\n\t\tppr := *pr\n\t\ttrk[id] = &ppr\n\t}\n\treturn checkAndReturn(cfg, trk)\n}\n\n// checkAndReturn calls checkInvariants on the input and returns either the\n// resulting error or the input.\n// Copyright 2019 The etcd Authors\n//\n// Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");\n// you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.\n// You may obtain a copy of the License at\n//\n//     http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n//\n// Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n// distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\n// WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\n// See the License for the specific language governing permissions and\n// limitations under the License.\n\npackage confchange\n\nimport (\n\tpb \"go.etcd.io/raft/v3/raftpb\"\n\t\"go.etcd.io/raft/v3/tracker\"\n)\n\n// toConfChangeSingle translates a conf state into 1) a slice of operations creating\n// first the config that will become the outgoing one, and then the incoming one, and\n// b) another slice that, when applied to the config resulted from 1), represents the\n// ConfState.\nfunc toConfChangeSingle(cs pb.ConfState) (out []pb.ConfChangeSingle, in []pb.ConfChangeSingle) {\n\t// Example to follow along this code:\n\t// voters=(1 2 3) learners=(5) outgoing=(1 2 4 6) learners_next=(4)\n\t//\n\t// This means that before entering the joint config, the configuration\n\t// had voters (1 2 4 6) and perhaps some learners that are already gone.\n\t// The new set of voters is (1 2 3), i.e. (1 2) were kept around, and (4 6)\n\t// are no longer voters; however 4 is poised to become a learner upon leaving\n\t// the joint state.\n\t// We can't tell whether 5 was a learner before entering the joint config,\n\t// but it doesn't matter (we'll pretend that it wasn't).\n\t//\n\t// The code below will construct\n\t// outgoing = add 1; add 2; add 4; add 6\n\t// incoming = remove 1; remove 2; remove 4; remove 6\n\t//            add 1;    add 2;    add 3;\n\t//            add-learner 5;\n\t//            add-learner 4;\n\t//\n\t// So, when starting with an empty config, after applying 'outgoing' we have\n\t//\n\t//   quorum=(1 2 4 6)\n\t//\n\t// From which we enter a joint state via 'incoming'\n\t//\n\t//   quorum=(1 2 3)&&(1 2 4 6) learners=(5) learners_next=(4)\n\t//\n\t// as desired.\n\n\tfor _, id := range cs.VotersOutgoing {\n\t\t// If there are outgoing voters, first add them one by one so that the\n\t\t// (non-joint) config has them all.\n\t\tout = append(out, pb.ConfChangeSingle{\n\t\t\tType:   pb.ConfChangeAddNode,\n\t\t\tNodeID: id,\n\t\t})\n\n\t}\n\n\t// We're done constructing the outgoing slice, now on to the incoming one\n\t// (which will apply on top of the config created by the outgoing slice).\n\n\t// First, we'll remove all of the outgoing voters.\n\tfor _, id := range cs.VotersOutgoing {\n\t\tin = append(in, pb.ConfChangeSingle{\n\t\t\tType:   pb.ConfChangeRemoveNode,\n\t\t\tNodeID: id,\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\t// Then we'll add the incoming voters and learners.\n\tfor _, id := range cs.Voters {\n\t\tin = append(in, pb.ConfChangeSingle{\n\t\t\tType:   pb.ConfChangeAddNode,\n\t\t\tNodeID: id,\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\tfor _, id := range cs.Learners {\n\t\tin = append(in, pb.ConfChangeSingle{\n\t\t\tType:   pb.ConfChangeAddLearnerNode,\n\t\t\tNodeID: id,\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\t// Same for LearnersNext; these are nodes we want to be learners but which\n\t// are currently voters in the outgoing config.\n\tfor _, id := range cs.LearnersNext {\n\t\tin = append(in, pb.ConfChangeSingle{\n\t\t\tType:   pb.ConfChangeAddLearnerNode,\n\t\t\tNodeID: id,\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\treturn out, in\n}\n\nfunc chain(chg Changer, ops ...func(Changer) (tracker.Config, tracker.ProgressMap, error)) (tracker.Config, tracker.ProgressMap, error) {\n\tfor _, op := range ops {\n\t\tcfg, trk, err := op(chg)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn tracker.Config{}, nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tchg.Tracker.Config = cfg\n\t\tchg.Tracker.Progress = trk\n\t}\n\treturn chg.Tracker.Config, chg.Tracker.Progress, nil\n}\n\n// Restore takes a Changer (which must represent an empty configuration), and\n// runs a sequence of changes enacting the configuration described in the\n// ConfState.\n//\n// TODO(tbg) it's silly that this takes a Changer. Unravel this by making sure\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_submission.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nsources=[]\ndef src(id,file,start,end,kind='code_observation'):\n sources.append(dict(id=id,file=file,start_line=start,end_line=end,kind=kind));return id\nsrc('s_usage','doc.go',29,207,'interface_statement')\nsrc('s_ready_contract','node.go',49,112,'interface_statement')\nsrc('s_node_contract','node.go',134,229,'interface_statement')\nsrc('s_node_loop','node.go',336,455)\nsrc('s_raw_init','rawnode.go',31,127)\nsrc('s_ready','rawnode.go',130,190)\nsrc('s_append_completion','rawnode.go',202,366)\nsrc('s_apply_completion','rawnode.go',368,495)\nsrc('s_storage_contract','storage.go',35,90,'interface_statement')\nsrc('s_init','raft.go',437,496)\nsrc('s_send','raft.go',510,600)\nsrc('s_replication_send','raft.go',603,738)\nsrc('s_applied','raft.go',740,775)\nsrc('s_reset_append','raft.go',778,847)\nsrc('s_ticks_roles','raft.go',850,993)\nsrc('s_campaign','raft.go',995,1083)\nsrc('s_dispatch','raft.go',1085,1264)\nsrc('s_proposal_read','raft.go',1267,1377)\nsrc('s_ack','raft.go',1500,1596)\nsrc('s_transfer','raft.go',1597,1664)\nsrc('s_follow_roles','raft.go',1668,1774)\nsrc('s_recovery','raft.go',1786,1945)\nsrc('s_config','raft.go',1947,2031)\nsrc('s_abort','raft.go',2053,2059)\nsrc('s_read_release','raft.go',2062,2085)\nsrc('s_read_queue_release','raft.go',2123,2162)\nsrc('s_log_append','log.go',107,143)\nsrc('s_log_apply','log.go',218,273)\nsrc('s_log_commit_apply','log.go',320,363)\nsrc('s_log_matching','log.go',440,469)\nsrc('s_stable','log_unstable.go',134,162)\nsrc('s_tracker','tracker/tracker.go',148,217)\nsrc('s_votes','tracker/tracker.go',245,282)\nsrc('s_joint','quorum/joint.go',17,78)\nsrc('s_majority','quorum/majority.go',108,205)\nsrc('s_changer','confchange/confchange.go',35,269)\nsrc('s_conf_invariants','confchange/confchange.go',273,347)\nsrc('s_joint_contract','raftpb/raft.proto',118,134,'interface_statement')\nsrc('s_conf_contract','raftpb/raft.proto',178,214,'interface_statement')\nsrc('s_conf_decode','raftpb/confchange.go',77,113)\nsrc('s_readonly','read_only.go',19,132)\nB=[]\ndef b(id,a,owner,ctx,trigger,ss,**kw):\n B.append(dict(id=id,primary_activity=a,execution_owner=owner,protocol_context=ctx,trigger=trigger,source_ids=ss,**kw))\nb('b_formation','A1','raft leader and follower Step handlers','Leader term, log index and active voter configuration','Proposal appends; MsgApp validates predecessor; MsgAppResp advances tracked Match and attempts commit',['s_proposal_read','s_reset_append','s_ack','s_replication_send','s_log_append','s_log_matching','s_tracker','s_joint','s_majority'],implementation_guards=['Leader rejects proposals during transfer or after removal; pending configuration proposals become empty normal entries when validation fails.','Follower rejects mismatching predecessor; conflicting committed entries cause panic.','Commit advancement requires the quorum index to have current leader term.'],writes=['Leader assigns term/index and appends unstable entries; peer Match advances on accepted replies.','Follower commit is bounded by the append match; heartbeat producer caps commit at peer Match.'],external_effects=['Leader broadcasts on append and commit; retry probing follows rejection.'],async_boundaries=['Local self-ack and remote append replies are queued through persistence completion.'],produces_fact_ids=['f_commit'],unknowns=[])\nb('b_authority','A2','raft Step, campaign and role transitions','Term, role, current voter configuration and election lease','Campaign/Tick; term-bearing network message; vote reply or quorum check',['s_ticks_roles','s_campaign','s_dispatch','s_follow_roles','s_reset_append','s_votes','s_joint','s_majority','s_log_matching'],implementation_guards=['Campaign requires promotable membership, no pending snapshot and no committed unapplied configuration changes.','Grant vote only when vote/leader permits and candidate log is up to date; pre-vote does not itself change term.','Vote counting uses configured voters, with both majorities in joint state; response type must match candidate phase.'],writes=['Reset clears votes, remote Match, readOnly heartbeat acknowledgments and transfer state; new term clears Vote.','Leader appends a current-term empty entry and conservatively sets pendingConfIndex to prior tail.'],important_branches=['Higher-term messages generally force follower role except pre-vote cases and lease-filtered vote requests.','Lower-term messages are ignored except explicit responses to stale leaders and snapshot completion from old storage replies.','Reset does not clear pendingReadIndexMessages; these are distinct from readOnly heartbeat acknowledgments.'],consumes_fact_ids=['f_commit'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Term filtering and reset prevent ordinary old-term append responses from contributing to a new leader quorum; established committed prefix is retained.'},unknowns=[])\nb('b_persistence','A6','RawNode Ready/Advance and caller storage workers','Ordered Ready batches, storage append term and entry identity','Ready emission and caller completion response',['s_ready_contract','s_ready','s_append_completion','s_apply_completion','s_dispatch','s_stable','s_send','s_storage_contract'],legal_preconditions=['Serialize RawNode access; honor Ready persistence order or reliable ordered local append messages; return responses after corresponding work.'],writes=['Accepted work is marked in progress; stableTo removes matching unstable entries only.'],durable_effects=['Durability is performed by the caller; the implementation queues dependent votes and append acknowledgments.'],important_branches=['Synchronous mode places external responses in Ready and local responses on Advance.','Async mode attaches dependent responses to append work, including when no new entries exist.','Stale-term append completion cannot stabilize entries, but may complete a committed snapshot. New-term HardState work carries another stability acknowledgment.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Defers counting persistence-dependent support until completion.','A2':'Term-scoped storage acknowledgments avoid discarding unstable state after overwrites across leaders.'},unknowns=[])\nb('b_application','A5','RawNode, raft.appliedTo, caller apply worker','Committed/application indexes and active configuration','Ready committed entries, Advance or MsgStorageApplyResp, snapshot completion',['s_apply_completion','s_log_apply','s_log_commit_apply','s_applied','s_node_contract'],consumes_fact_ids=['f_commit','f_joint'],implementation_guards=['Committed entries are withheld while snapshot work is pending; async application is bounded by local stable index.','Application accounting is bounded by committed index; raft.appliedTo uses max to accommodate snapshot/application overlap.'],writes=['Tracks applying/applied indexes and outstanding bytes.'],external_effects=['Offers committed entries to caller; when AutoLeave and applied>=pendingConfIndex and leader, proposes an empty configuration change.'],important_branches=['Automatic exit proposal uses ordinary Step and can be dropped during transfer; retry currently occurs on another appliedTo call.'],async_boundaries=['Application worker completion is independent of append worker; responses are term-independent.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Applying membership changes changes which stored acknowledgments qualify for future commitment.','A2':'Application completion can initiate automatic exit from joint membership.'},unknowns=['Whether failed automatic exit during transfer is guaranteed another applicable completion trigger after transfer aborts.'])\nb('b_membership','A4','raft.applyConfChange, switchToConfig and confchange.Changer','Applied configuration, incoming/outgoing voters, staged learners','Caller applies a committed ConfChange or restore installs ConfState',['s_config','s_changer','s_conf_invariants','s_conf_contract','s_joint_contract','s_conf_decode'],produces_fact_ids=['f_joint','f_commit'],consumes_fact_ids=['f_joint','f_commit'],implementation_guards=['Simple changes preserve at most one voter difference; joint changes preserve outgoing voters until exit.','Learners cannot simultaneously belong to voter sets; staged demotions retain outgoing-voter participation.'],writes=['Updates voter sets, progress membership and AutoLeave; preserves eligible existing peer progress.'],external_effects=['switchToConfig recomputes commitment and broadcasts on advancement, otherwise probes peers; removed transferee aborts transfer.'],important_branches=['Leader removal/demotion steps down only when configured; proposal admission independently checks membership.','The configuration commit path does not call releasePendingReadIndexMessages, unlike the append-response path.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Reinterprets peer Match under the new quorum and can advance commit.','A2':'Changes eligibility to campaign or remain leader and the active quorum authority.'},unknowns=['Whether read requests deferred before first current-term commit can remain pending after a configuration-induced commit; caller ReadIndex retries are explicitly required.'])\nb('b_transfer','A2','raft stepLeader and tickHeartbeat','Current leader and configured non-learner transferee','TransferLeader, replication catching transferee up, timeout or configuration removal',['s_transfer','s_ticks_roles','s_abort','s_config','s_proposal_read'],writes=['Sets leadTransferee and resets electionElapsed; abort only clears leadTransferee.'],external_effects=['Sends TimeoutNow when transferee matches local tail; otherwise sends append.'],important_branches=['Drops proposals while transfer active.','At election timeout, continuing leader aborts transfer; successful new leader appends an empty entry through role transition.'],consumes_fact_ids=['f_joint'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Temporarily prevents ordinary and automatic configuration proposals from entering the log.'},unknowns=['Does any independently scheduled work reattempt automatic joint exit if transfer times out after all entry application is complete?'])\nb('b_recovery','A3','raft restore, follower append and leader progress machinery','Snapshot index/term, matching log, membership and peer replication state','Append rejection, missing compacted history, snapshot reception or report',['s_init','s_recovery','s_replication_send','s_transfer','s_log_append','s_log_matching'],produces_fact_ids=['f_commit','f_joint'],implementation_guards=['Snapshot at or below committed is ignored; recipient must appear in snapshot configuration.','Matching snapshot boundary fast-forwards commit without reinstalling snapshot; otherwise log and configuration are restored.'],external_effects=['Missing history sends snapshot only for recently active peer; temporary unavailability defers it.','Heartbeat responses reopen flow control and probe; snapshot status returns progress to probe.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Restores committed prefix or obtains fresh append support after resynchronization.','A2':'Pending snapshot prevents campaigning; snapshot configuration replaces eligibility.'},unknowns=['Detailed recovery of concurrent snapshot and apply work remains outside the initial backbone.'])\nb('b_reads','A7','raft read-only request/reply handlers and caller','Request context, leader term, commit index and quorum heartbeat acknowledgments','ReadIndex request, current-term commit or heartbeat response',['s_node_contract','s_proposal_read','s_readonly','s_ack','s_read_release','s_read_queue_release','s_follow_roles','s_reset_append'],consumes_fact_ids=['f_commit'],implementation_guards=['Non-singleton leaders defer until a current-term entry is committed.','ReadOnlySafe aggregates heartbeat acknowledgments under active quorum; follower accepts one-entry response after term dispatch.'],writes=['Queues deferred requests separately from readOnly pending heartbeat requests; reset replaces the latter.'],external_effects=['Returns ReadState or MsgReadIndexResp; caller correlates RequestCtx and waits for application.'],important_branches=['Singleton path bypasses quorum heartbeat round; lease-based path depends on its separate configuration assumptions.','Read requests can be lost; Node contract assigns retries to caller.'],unknowns=['Effects of retained pre-commit requests across authority and membership changes require narrower histories.'])\nF=[dict(id='f_commit',meaning='The local raftLog has established a committed prefix through its committed index; commitment is separate from local persistence and application completion.',identity={'owner':'Raft instance','position':'Log prefix ending at committed index'},validity_context='Retained across term changes; established by current-term leader quorum, leader append/heartbeat information, or accepted snapshot under the respective guards.',representation=['raftLog.committed'],durability='Exported as HardState.Commit; persistence is caller-owned.',recovery='newRaft loads stored HardState and snapshot/log boundaries; snapshot restoration may advance the prefix.',source_ids=['s_init','s_log_matching','s_log_append','s_replication_send','s_recovery','s_config'],unknowns=[]),dict(id='f_joint',meaning='The active configuration retains incoming and outgoing voter sets with AutoLeave indicating that Raft is assigned to initiate exit; the flag does not attest that an exit proposal has been accepted.',identity={'owner':'Raft instance','configuration':'Applied membership transition represented by ConfState'},validity_context='From installing joint configuration until leave-joint application or replacement through recovery; leader term may change while membership remains joint.',representation=['trk.Config.Voters','trk.Config.AutoLeave','ConfState'],durability='Configuration is reconstructed from caller-provided ConfState and applied configuration history.',recovery='newRaft/restore install configuration through confchange.Restore; AutoLeave is part of ConfState.',source_ids=['s_config','s_changer','s_init','s_recovery','s_joint_contract','s_conf_contract'],unknowns=[])]\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nacts=[]\nfor a in roles:\n bs=[x for x in B if x['primary_activity']==a]\n acts.append(dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=roles[a]['relation'],realization_summary=' '.join(x['trigger'] for x in bs),source_ids=list(dict.fromkeys(s for x in bs for s in x['source_ids']))))\nformation='A caller proposes through RawNode/Node. The leader assigns term/index, appends unstable entries and replicates with predecessor identity. Followers require matching predecessor, refuse committed conflicts, and queue append replies after persistence. The leader self-acks after its persistence completion and aggregates peer Match using active voter majority (both halves for joint configuration); only a quorum index in its current term directly advances commitment. Append messages and Match-capped heartbeats propagate commitment. Ready exposes committed work; the caller applies entries in order and applies configuration entries. Advance or async application replies account for completion. Rejections probe backward, heartbeats reopen flow control, and compacted history uses snapshots.'\ncontext='A promotable node with no unapplied committed configuration changes campaigns, optionally with pre-vote. Votes require eligible vote state and an up-to-date candidate log; configured voter quorums determine election. Term dispatch rejects stale replies and usually steps down on higher terms, with pre-vote/lease exceptions. Reset clears vote aggregation, replication progress, read-only heartbeat support and transfer state while preserving the committed prefix. Storage replies are term-scoped for entry stabilization, but committed snapshot/application completion survives term changes. Transfer suppresses proposals until success, abort or timeout. Applied configuration changes alter voter eligibility; snapshots/restart restore membership and history.'\nconnection='The term and active configuration jointly qualify support: a leader consumes only current-context responses from tracked participants, while quorum evaluation selects voters and joint majorities. Membership application can reinterpret existing Match and advance commitment without a new reply. A new leader resets remote Match, appends a new-term empty entry, and cannot campaign past known unapplied configuration changes. Pending read heartbeat support is reset, but the separate pre-commit read queue survives reset. Applying a joint configuration sets AutoLeave; application completion may propose its exit, while concurrent transfer may reject that proposal. Established decisions remain a prefix through authority changes; persistence and application completion have distinct response rules.'\nmapdoc=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Go raft module: Node/RawNode state machine, quorum/tracker/configuration and in-memory storage support; caller supplies durable storage, transport, regular ticks and application execution.',protocol_contexts=['Raft instance identity, term, role, log prefix and active membership'],external_interfaces=['Node','RawNode','Storage','Ready and local storage messages'],ownership=['Node goroutine serializes state; RawNode requires caller serialization.','Caller owns durable writes, transport and state-machine application.'],source_ids=['s_raw_init','s_node_loop','s_usage','s_storage_contract']),activities=acts,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='raft.appliedTo / abortLeaderTransfer',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b_application','b_transfer'],reason='Automatic exit rejected during transfer may require a later application event; identify whether caller duties or an internal retry guarantees that event.',source_ids=['s_applied','s_abort','s_ticks_roles','s_joint_contract'],high_consequence=True),dict