aller retry; implicit exit ownership must be distinguished from generic proposal semantics.'],unknowns=['Whether the documented implicit exit responsibility requires retry without further client proposals after a failed transfer.','Whether a legal producer history can leave no pending application work when the transfer aborts.','Whether timers, duplicate responses, configuration events or other internal paths retry independently of a later applied entry.'],trigger_rationale='The implicit-transition API assigns exit to Raft. appliedTo explicitly admits transfer rejection and relies on a next advance, while abortLeaderTransfer only clears a field. Inspect all callers and pending-work production before choosing a controlled execution; this is more discriminating than testing already composed durability guards or the ReadIndex path whose caller retry duty is explicit.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='source_review',priority=2)\nsub=dict(action='continue',rationale='Establish both core relationships and retain a sourced continuation question before claiming an obligation or running a check.',sources=sources,map_path='initial-map.json',question=question)\njson.dump(sub,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python build_submission.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
